  "description": "Three unequal lakes, a birch terrace, a Cut-gated pond island and a long Cedar Lake shoreline. The island shore rails and a visible water rock prevent Surf from bypassing its Cut-controlled bridge approach. The short main road crosses a railed inlet bridge; the longer east-bank circuit crosses marsh grass and rewards the walker with a fishing pier and Ether. Long Lake offers its narrow grass bank or a longer fishing shore. A native downhill ledge returns from the medicine/trainer terrace. Required regional travel needs neither Cut nor Surf.",
